 the way people look at  medication  yeah we are there's only two countries  on earth it's united states and new  zealand that allow prescription  medication to be marketed directly to  consumers and i think it's a bad thing  in that it does convey that message of  there is a pill for everything and you  should be taking it and ask your doctor  about it and you know i could never  prove that it's not like we can randomly  assign countries to um advertising  campaigns but i i personally think that  is part of the the problem of looking to  pills for everything including to solve  deep structural problems in the economy  for example or in society  that really need to be managed at a  different level than patient by patient  keith humphreys professor of psychiatry  and behavioral sciences at stanford  university professor we appreciate your  time and your valuable insights tonight  thank you  thank you
 

